{
 "_": [
  "Every hotspot family the house can build into. THE ONLY HAND-MADE FILE IN THE FURNITURE",
  "PIPELINE - tools/genfurn.py turns it into the enum tables, the varps, the constants and all of",
  "poh_furniture.rs2.",
  "",
  "  key      the ^poh_fam_<key> constant, and the order families are numbered in. NEVER REORDER:",
  "           the family number is not stored, but the ITEM number is, and item numbers follow",
  "           family order. Append only.",
  "  label    what the Furniture creation menu puts in its title bar",
  "  room     which room the hotspots are in, for the docs and for battery check 28",
  "  hotspots hotspot loc ids, checked against the six template squares",
  "  shape    the locshape every piece of this family is placed with - it has to be the shape its",
  "           hotspot carries in the template, or loc_add lands on a different layer and the",
  "           hotspot is not replaced",
  "  locs     the buildable locs, in tier order. Each must carry op5=Remove in poh.loc.",
  "  planks   how many planks a piece costs, the same at every tier, as OSRS mostly does",
  "  base     the family's base Construction level; a tier costs base + 7 per wood step + 3 per",
  "           tier within that wood",
  "",
  "NOT WIRED, and why: rugs, curtains, windows, floor decor and the combat ring are multi-tile",
  "assemblies of 6 to 19 hotspots that per-piece storage is the wrong shape for; the portal chamber",
  "needs a frame-then-destination flow of its own; the garden's centrepiece is where the exit portal",
  "stands; wall decorations and mounted shields are 48 locs each and need a menu that pages by",
  "material first; and the costume room's storage units have no locs in the 474 import."
 ],
